A||||10||Cliff Pennock||Automatic and weird shifting
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||05-05-99||12:53 PM||||Hey all,<p>My 86.5 GT Automatic does some weird things since a few days. Often when I step on the gas a little, it downshifts for a second (like it thinks I do a kickdown), then upshifts, then downshifts again etc... It sometimes does this 3-4 times before it stays in the higher gear.<p>Is this a kickdown cable problem?
Z||000001||theogre||05-05-99||02:17 PM||||I assume you checked the trany fluid??? what color is the fluid? is there allot of fine metal flake in it? does it smell burnt or otherwise abnormal?<p>if it's doing this when you floor it, you could have a kick down cable binding or a bad return spring. check the cable from the throtle body to the tranny really carefully.<p>beyond that, and maybe a band ajustment,,, there's not much you can do to it w/o pulling it. TH125 is a pretty solid tranny, but when it dies, it dies ugly allot of the time especially in v6 aplications that can pound it pretty hard.<p>if there's allot of metal, really dark oil, or bad smell, then the tranny should be taken to someone who can check it out good.... any of those things could indicate a clutch pack, or band, is failing. Either of those will fail from simple aging, but you could have other problems that would toast them to. (like a bad apply piston, clogged valve body, etc.)
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||05-05-99||02:59 PM||||Last time I checked the tranny fluid, it was crystal clear (or as clear as tranny fluid can be). I haven't checked it lately. The weird shifting does not occur when I floor it, but when I accelerate a little (and even then not always). It's just like the car can't make up its mind; whether to downshift or not, so it downshift for a second then upshift, then downshift again, etc. This can get very annoying (not to mention dangerous) when I accelerate when coming out of a corner because it shakes the car quite a bit.<p>But I'll check the tranny fluid again tomorrow.
Z||000003||theogre||05-05-99||03:24 PM||||clear? unless tranny fluid in Holland is usually clear that's not the right color. It's suposed to be a transparant red. Only very old fluid, where the dye has oxidized out, could be clear. Clear doesn't mean it's bad, but it's way old and you should probably flush the thing out. <p>Check the level... low even a little can do odd things. and check the cable to the throtle anyways, as well as the shifter cable. if either is flaky or out of adjustment you could have wierd problems.<p>To flush it you need to do a pan/filter kit, and drain the torq. The catch is that most TC's don't have a drain plug. That means doing a flush with a bunch of oil until you purge out as much old stuff as you can. You flush by disconecting one of the lines to the cooler. In Fiero's case, because the cooler is so far away, you want to disconnect the return line from the cooler so you get all that oil out to. (I'll look up wich line is which later. I have some other links on TH125 you might want as well but they are home.....)
Z||000004||Carrolles||05-05-99||03:59 PM||||I looked at my 85 Helms manual for your symptoms.  It says to check the Throttle Valve (T.V.) cable for proper adjustment or binding.  Everything else required getting into the trans case.  It also mentioned a sticking valve. <br>My daughter had an 86 Pontiac 6000 with the 2.8L V-6 and the TH125 transmission.  She got broadsided in a Mall parking lot one evening.  After that the trans acted up.  Sometimes it did what yours is doing and at other times it refused to upshift to 3rd or it simply skipped 2nd altogether.  I took it to an AAMCO shop.  They took it around the block and then looked at the dip stick.  The mechanic said the fluid was all burned up and the trans needed rebuilding.<br>I had just changed the trans fluid 2 weeks before and I knew it was not burned.<br>I took the car to a local mechanic and explained what had happened.  He put some Trans fluid conditioner/cleaner in and after a week it shifted like new.  It still works fine.  He explained that when the car got broadsided it probable shook loose some crud in the trans that got lodged in the shift valves.  $3.00 fixed my problem.<br>Maybe yours is getting sludged up.<br>Hope this helps<br>Carroll
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||05-05-99||05:17 PM||||Well, the car <b>has been</b> in an accident a few weeks ago... I got hit by a van who wasn't paying any attention.<p>Ogre, I meant to say the fluid indeed had a reddish color but it showed no sign of contamination whatsoever. So I meant to say it was "a-reddish-crystal clear". ;)<p>Anyway, thanks for all the tips, I'll check it out tomorrow.
Z||000006||kel||05-12-99||02:15 AM||||Cliff,<br>I was just wondering if you tried Carrolles suggestion about the transmission fluid cleaner?  My 86SE automatic was doing the same thing.  The trans fluid cleaner worked like a charm.
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||05-12-99||04:18 PM||||No I haven't tried it yet, I just got my car back today from repairs. I will look into the problem further on friday. I'll let you know.
Z||000008||theogre||05-12-99||05:51 PM||||what brands of cleaners do you both use? 
Z||000009||Cliff Pennock||05-15-99||04:46 PM||||Well, like duh! I checked the tranny fluid level and guess what? It just needed a pint of fluid and now all is ok... Item number umphty on the list of stupid things to forget...
Z||000010||theogre||05-15-99||06:05 PM||||.......... twit. :)
